WEBVTT

NOTE
Fallback recording of /demo steps 3 to 7 (issue #3478): connect an agent,
approve its budget, buy a joke, try to overspend. Text mirrors the /demo
page and the refusal body Haven's API returns.

00:00.000 --> 00:04.000
See a Haven agent pay. Steps 3 to 7 of the /demo walk, about one minute.
Test funds only: Base Sepolia test network.

00:04.000 --> 00:09.500
Step 3, connect an agent. On the Agents page, the connect flow asks for a
budget before anything is wired up. This demo sets 0.05 USDC per day, well
under the 1 USDC send the last step tries.

00:09.500 --> 00:15.000
The flow hands back a setup prompt to paste into Claude Code, Codex, or
Hermes. The agent runs the connector, which creates its signing key locally
and sends Haven only the public address.

00:15.000 --> 00:22.000
Step 4, approve the budget with your passkey. Nothing the agent does is
authorized until you sign. The signature grants the 0.05 USDC daily budget;
there is no Haven approval queue behind it.

00:22.000 --> 00:33.000
Step 5, check that it is connected. Ask the agent what your Haven budget is.
It calls haven_get_agent: 0.05 USDC per day, about 0.049 USDC remaining
today. The Haven tools are loaded.

00:33.000 --> 00:45.000
Step 6, buy a joke. The agent calls haven_pay for Ampersend's joke offer at
0.001 USDC. The offer answers 402 Payment Required, the agent signs the
EIP-3009 payment intent, and the merchant accepts it: well inside the
budget, so no approval step is needed at this size.

00:45.000 --> 00:57.000
Step 7, try to overspend. Ask the agent to send 1 USDC. Haven refuses it
before any money moves: over the agent's remaining budget, short by 0.951
USDC. There is no approval queue; an over-budget redemption reverts
on-chain. Retrying cannot succeed.

00:57.000 --> 01:03.000
What you just saw: an agent paid from a budget its user signed and could
not exceed, and a payment over that budget was refused before it could
move. Every limit is enforced by the Haven account itself, on-chain.
